* GITFURNITURE - the engine op, as a SUBROUTINE.  See qm/BP/GIT.QM.
*
* One line of glue, exactly as jBASE's DEFC wrappers are: the handlers in BP/
* call these by name on their ENGINE arm, so the same handler source works
* here unchanged.  All the CCALL machinery is in GIT.QM.
*
* THE WORD THE PREPROCESSOR READS IS NOT WRITTEN IN THIS COMMENT, deliberately.
* A conditional directive inside a comment is a portability trap of its own,
* and the suite greps for sources that TEST a symbol without including
* PLATFORM.H -- which a comment naming one would fail, for no reason.
*
* THE REPOSITORY IS SUPPLIED HERE, NOT PASSED IN.  GIT.OBJ calls this op with
* the candidate list alone, because the engine half takes only a list -- the
* furniture rules are the engine's, not a repository's.  The bridge still wants
* argument one to be the repository, as it is for every other op, so the
* wrapper names it; MVX's C half hardcodes the same ".git" for the same reason.
      SUBROUTINE GITFURNITURE(LIST, ANS)
      CALL GIT.QM("FURNITURE", ".git", LIST, "", "", "", ANS)
      RETURN
END
